<!-- SERVICE CARDS -->
<section style="padding:0 24px 80px;background:#EAF5FB;">
  <div style="max-width:1100px;margin:0 auto;">
    <div class="svc-grid" style="display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(4,1fr);gap:20px;">
      <a href="/asbestos-fence-removal-geelong/" style="display:flex;flex-direction:column;background:#fff;border:1px solid #e3ded4;border-radius:12px;padding:30px 26px;text-decoration:none;box-shadow:0 2px 8px rgba(14,77,110,0.06);">
        <h3 style="font-family:'Nunito Sans',sans-serif;font-size:20px;font-weight:800;color:#0A3D5C;margin:0 0 10px;">Asbestos Fence Removal</h3>
        <p style="font-size:14.5px;line-height:1.7;color:#555;margin:0 0 18px;flex:1;">The old grey boundary fence is the most common asbestos job in Geelong's post war suburbs, and a weathered or cracked one matters more than an intact one. Published Victorian rates put a whole fence at $1,000 to $3,500, and a licensed removalist prices yours after seeing it.</p>
        <span style="font-size:13px;font-weight:700;color:#2FA34D;letter-spacing:0.04em;text-transform:uppercase;">Learn More &#8594;</span>
      </a>
      <a href="/asbestos-roof-removal-geelong/" style="display:flex;flex-direction:column;background:#fff;border:1px solid #e3ded4;border-radius:12px;padding:30px 26px;text-decoration:none;box-shadow:0 2px 8px rgba(14,77,110,0.06);">
        <h3 style="font-family:'Nunito Sans',sans-serif;font-size:20px;font-weight:800;color:#0A3D5C;margin:0 0 10px;">Asbestos Roof & Shed Removal</h3>
        <p style="font-size:14.5px;line-height:1.7;color:#555;margin:0 0 18px;flex:1;">Super Six roofing, garage and shed cladding and eaves linings, taken down without water blasting, drilling, dry sweeping or walking on the sheets. Victorian rates run $40 to $120 per square metre, with a house roof at $4,000 to $15,000 and a single garage at $2,500 to $5,000.</p>
        <span style="font-size:13px;font-weight:700;color:#2FA34D;letter-spacing:0.04em;text-transform:uppercase;">Learn More &#8594;</span>
      </a>
      <a href="/asbestos-testing-geelong/" style="display:flex;flex-direction:column;background:#fff;border:1px solid #e3ded4;border-radius:12px;padding:30px 26px;text-decoration:none;box-shadow:0 2px 8px rgba(14,77,110,0.06);">
        <h3 style="font-family:'Nunito Sans',sans-serif;font-size:20px;font-weight:800;color:#0A3D5C;margin:0 0 10px;">Asbestos Testing & Identification</h3>
        <p style="font-size:14.5px;line-height:1.7;color:#555;margin:0 0 18px;flex:1;">Nobody can tell asbestos from ordinary fibre cement by eye, and under Victoria's OHS Regulations only a laboratory approved by NATA can identify it. Analysis runs $88 to $160 per sample with a written result in 1 to 5 business days.</p>
        <span style="font-size:13px;font-weight:700;color:#2FA34D;letter-spacing:0.04em;text-transform:uppercase;">Learn More &#8594;</span>
      </a>
      <a href="/asbestos-disposal-geelong/" style="display:flex;flex-direction:column;background:#fff;border:1px solid #e3ded4;border-radius:12px;padding:30px 26px;text-decoration:none;box-shadow:0 2px 8px rgba(14,77,110,0.06);">
        <h3 style="font-family:'Nunito Sans',sans-serif;font-size:20px;font-weight:800;color:#0A3D5C;margin:0 0 10px;">Asbestos Disposal & Skip Hire</h3>
        <p style="font-size:14.5px;line-height:1.7;color:#555;margin:0 0 18px;flex:1;">Asbestos waste is reportable priority waste under Victoria's Environment Protection Regulations, so it can only go to a landfill authorised to receive it. It never goes in a general skip or a council hard waste collection, and every package has to be wrapped in 200 micron polythene and carry the warning mark.</p>
        <span style="font-size:13px;font-weight:700;color:#2FA34D;letter-spacing:0.04em;text-transform:uppercase;">Learn More &#8594;</span>
      </a>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
